  "name": "Pokémon Snap Photo Contest (CoroCoro Comic)",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "In 1999 CoroCoro Comic and Nintendo's TV show 64 Mario Stadium each ran a Best Photo Contest for Pokémon Snap, which came out on the Nintendo 64 in Japan on 21 March 1999. Players printed their photos as stickers at Lawson convenience stores and mailed one in on a postcard, and five winners from each contest had their photo made into a card, credited \"Photo.\" where a card names its illustrator. CoroCoro's five, announced in its August 1999 issue, were Bulbasaur, Pikachu, Poliwag, Magikarp and Gyarados; they have a camera in place of a set symbol, and a bottom edge naming them \"Best Photo Contest\" prize cards.\n\nEach winner was sent 20 copies of their card in November 1999, with a letter from Media Factory, after lending Nintendo the game cartridge that held the photo. Some have reached collectors, among them 15 Poliwag its winner sold and probably spares sold by Yuichi Konno, one of the card game's original developers, but Pikachu and Magikarp have hardly surfaced at all.",
    "sources": [
